WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:05.480
Clocking in at two hours and thirty-five minutes,
The Last Jedi is easily the longest of the

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:06.670
Star Wars films.

00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:10.450
But there were still a lot of important scenes
that ended up on the cutting room floor, with

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:15.070
director Rian Johnson promising 20 minutes
of deleted scenes when the Blu-ray comes out.

00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:16.590
So what can fans expect?

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:21.730
Here's a spoiler-filled peek at the Last Jedi
scenes you didn't see.

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:22.730
Bromance

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:27.080
Early in The Last Jedi, fans got to see a
brief reunion between Poe Dameron and Finn

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:30.999
after the former stormtrooper woke up from
his medically induced coma.

00:00:30.999 --> 00:00:35.690
Originally, though, there was a longer sequence
where Poe brings Finn up to speed on what's

00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:37.930
happened to the Resistance since he was injured.

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:43.100
Editor Bob Ducsay told Slash Film that fans
of the bromance will love it, saying,

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:45.960
"It's a really, really good character scene.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:48.890
The only reason it's not in the movie is just
because of time.

00:00:48.890 --> 00:00:51.040
I really love that scene."

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:53.040
Hey, flyboy

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:57.970
Before Vice Admiral Holdo proved herself by
heroically sacrificing her life to save the

00:00:57.970 --> 00:01:02.410
Rebellion, fans weren't quite sure what to
think of her thanks to her combative relationship

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:03.410
with Poe.

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:07.400
Originally, though, she was apparently much
worse, to the point where Johnson cut some

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:12.060
of their scenes together and had actress Laura
Dern re-record her dialogue in others to make

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:13.190
her less condescending.

00:01:13.190 --> 00:01:17.550
Though, to be fair, Poe totally had it coming
after his terrible plan nearly doomed the

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:19.790
entire galaxy.

00:01:19.790 --> 00:01:21.290
Love triangle

00:01:21.290 --> 00:01:26.690
Whether you ship Finn and Rose, Finn and Poe,
or Finn and Rey, there's one deleted scene

00:01:26.690 --> 00:01:31.330
of particular interest, where Rose and Finn
discuss Finn's feelings for Rey.

00:01:31.330 --> 00:01:36.270
When Rose, who clearly has a thing for Finn,
suggests he's pining for Rey, he denies it

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:40.750
and says that he was "raised to fight," but
that he had never found anything worth fighting

00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:44.660
for until Rey became his friend—emphasis
on friend.

00:01:44.660 --> 00:01:45.700
Hmm!

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:48.000
Going undercover

00:01:48.010 --> 00:01:52.130
Although Finn and Rose's storyline seems to
go on forever, it turns out originally it

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:56.700
was even longer, as a number of scenes in
their undercover mission aboard Snoke's Star

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:58.560
Destroyer ended up being cut.

00:01:58.560 --> 00:01:59.710
Johnson told Collider,

00:01:59.710 --> 00:02:04.860
"It's a full sequence of stuff with them sneaking
through this big office area of the Mega Destroyer

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:07.670
and then having to fake out these Stormtroopers."

00:02:07.670 --> 00:02:11.599
And one of those Stormtroopers was apparently
played by Tom Hardy, who originally had a

00:02:11.599 --> 00:02:14.209
speaking role that ended up on the cutting
room floor.

00:02:14.209 --> 00:02:19.510
According to Slash Film, Hardy's stormtrooper
has an American "southern" accent, and apparently

00:02:19.510 --> 00:02:22.109
is an acquaintance of Finn's from his First
Order days.

00:02:22.109 --> 00:02:26.469
When they run into each other on an elevator,
Hardy's stormtrooper stares at Finn for several

00:02:26.469 --> 00:02:29.599
seconds before blurting out, "I know who you
are….

00:02:29.599 --> 00:02:30.599
FN-2187!

00:02:30.599 --> 00:02:34.980
Damn boy, I never took you for officer material!"

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:36.790
Gunslinger Phasma

00:02:36.790 --> 00:02:41.319
Is there any character in the new trilogy
that has been as underserved as poor Captain

00:02:41.319 --> 00:02:42.319
Phasma?

00:02:42.319 --> 00:02:46.750
She looks cool, but gets nothing to do - except
when she's being tossed in a dumpster or killed

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:47.750
off.

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:51.219
But in a deleted scene, Phasma actually got
to be awesome for once.

00:02:51.219 --> 00:02:55.810
During Finn's mission aboard the Star Destroyer,
he tries to convince a squad of Stormtroopers

00:02:55.810 --> 00:02:59.711
to quit the First Order and join him in the
rebellion by revealing it was Phasma who gave

00:02:59.711 --> 00:03:03.439
him the codes to lower the shields to Starkiller
Base in The Force Awakens.

00:03:03.439 --> 00:03:07.749
Before the stormtroopers can make up their
minds, though, Phasma shows up, whips out

00:03:07.749 --> 00:03:11.769
her blaster, and mows down the entire unit
singlehandedly.

00:03:11.769 --> 00:03:13.200
Luke's third lesson

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:17.309
If you were keeping count while watching The
Last Jedi, you might've noticed that Luke

00:03:17.309 --> 00:03:21.279
never gave Rey his promised "third lesson"
during their Jedi training.

00:03:21.279 --> 00:03:25.389
Johnson has promised fans that this "massive
sequence" will appear in the deleted scenes

00:03:25.389 --> 00:03:27.669
when the Blu-ray drops in mid-2018.

00:03:27.669 --> 00:03:31.499
So what happens in this sequence, which was
teased in the trailer with a brief shot of

00:03:31.499 --> 00:03:33.529
Rey running across the beach?

00:03:33.529 --> 00:03:38.870
Essentially, Luke fakes an attack on the island,
seemingly putting innocents in danger to illustrate

00:03:38.870 --> 00:03:42.199
to Rey how outdated the Jedi's code of balance
is.

00:03:42.199 --> 00:03:47.620
Rey is not happy about the deception, though,
probably because all this stuff about non-interference

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:50.360
sounds just a little… too familiar.

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:54.340
"I'm bound by the rules of the United Federation
of Planets, which order me not to interfere

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:55.839
with other worlds, other cultures.

00:03:55.839 --> 00:04:00.239
If I were to tell them any of this, I'd violate
the Prime Directive."

00:04:00.239 --> 00:04:01.359
Thanks for watching!

00:04:01.359 --> 00:04:03.760
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:05.769
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

